    {
      "id": "02-create",
      "instruction": "In Odoo, go to the Sales app and create a new quotation for the customer '{{runid}} Bench Customer' (the customer field is an autocomplete dropdown — you must pick the matching option from the dropdown, not just type the name). Add exactly ONE order line: pick any product from the product catalogue using the product autocomplete dropdown (choose an actual option from the dropdown), with quantity 3. Let the app fill in the unit price automatically. Save the quotation and report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the unit price the app filled in, (c) the untaxed amount the app computes (shown in the totals area), and (d) the quotation's name/reference. Do not confirm the quotation yet. Note: the app long-polls so never wait for network idle; wait for concrete page state instead.",
      "outputs": [
        "product_name",
        "unit_price",
        "quantity",
        "taxes",
        "untaxed_amount",
        "tax_amount_20pct",
        "total",
        "customer_displayed",
        "quotation_reference",
        "saved",
        "confirmed"
      ],
